  v03 — refined crosshair test (known34c_0001)          May 24 16:04
----------------------------------------------------------------
  5 PNGs:  crosshair_known34c_0001_{hst, euvis, eunisp, jwst1, jwst2}.png

  WHAT:   Same single-source test but with two design changes:
          (a) Renamed tag from "known34" to "known34c" to mark a
              corrected / curated iteration.
          (b) Crosshair switched to a 4-case PARTIAL style: the arms
              that would land on the host galaxy are dropped; only the
              arms pointing AWAY from host are drawn.  This way the
              SN itself is never obscured.
          (c) Solid-line style for the detection panel, dashed for
              the non-detection panels (Task #42 in the task list).

  WHY:    Made the crosshair informative without hiding the data it
          is pointing at.

  STATUS: Crosshair style finalised here; remained the convention
          for v04.

