  v04 — polished 5-source set                          May 25 23:57
----------------------------------------------------------------
  25 PNGs:  polished_<id>_{hst, euvis, eunisp, jwst1, jwst2}.png
            for id ∈ {318858, 320233, 130972, 371996, 471959}

  WHAT:   First "publication-style" set.  Added a full polish layer:
            - 4-corner labels: top-left = ID + photo-z + SN sigma;
              top-left line 2 = survey + filter + host mag;
              bottom-left = SN mag line; bottom-right = 1″ scale bar
            - SN sigma label only on JWST panels (best-band σ)
            - Combined-σ cap at 50σ
            - SN-line hidden on non-detection panels
            - Host-mag suffix dropped when value unavailable
            - JWST cutouts rotated to North-up (compute roll from WCS)
            - SCI+ERR HDU access switched to v1.0 i2d for proper SNR
            - Aperture photometry: simple aper − host − ring-σ
            - All 5 spotlight SN (Point-5 user reference list) included

  WHY:    Intended as the final deliverable for the orphan-SN
          eyeball-validation deck.

  KNOWN ISSUE (BIG ONE): HST SN positions for the three HST-detected
          cases (130972, 371996, 471959) were WRONG.  We used
          user-supplied eyeball offsets verbatim instead of measuring
          the actual SN centroid.  The crosshair is offset 0.2–1.4″
          from the true SN in each case.  See v05.

----------------------------------------------------------------
  v05 — measured HST SN positions, simple crosshair    May 26 03:42
----------------------------------------------------------------
  15 PNGs:  sn_known34c_{0003, 0004, 0005}_{hst, euclid_vis,
                                            euclid_nisp, jwst1, jwst2}.png
            seq 0003 = ID 130972
            seq 0004 = ID 371996
            seq 0005 = ID 471959

  WHAT:   HST-only verification pass after the v04 position bug.
            - Opened each HST F814W tile, took a 1.0–1.5″ box around
              the user's refined eyeball hint
            - Ran a 2D-Gaussian-smoothed centroid (peak + intensity-
              weighted moments) to find the true SN position
            - All three measured positions landed within 0.05–0.18″
              of the user's eyeball hint (confirming the hint was a
              reasonable starting point, and that the centroid found
              the SN, not the host)
            - Re-cut all 5 panels per source at the MEASURED position
            - Added a simple green '+' crosshair at the cutout
              center (= measured SN position)
            - No polish labels (focused on validating position before
              re-doing the full label layer)

          Measured positions:
            130972  RA=150.279695  Dec=2.041101
            371996  RA=150.282844  Dec=1.932259
            471959  RA=150.278904  Dec=2.430962

  WHY:    Quick visual gate before the next polished iteration.

  PERFORMANCE NOTE: Whole 15-PNG re-cut ran in 22 seconds (vs.
          ~10–15 min on the v04 run) thanks to two script fixes:
            (1) Cutout2D slice BEFORE astype, so only the 80KB box
                is read from disk, not the full 500MB-30GB tile.
            (2) FITS handle caching by path (Euclid tile 101542818
                is shared by 130972 and 371996).
          Also benefited from OS page cache being warmed by the
          preceding centroid step.

  SCOPE:  Only the 3 HST SN.  JWST-only IDs (318858, 320233) and
          Euclid NISP-only ID (63924) were not re-cut in this round;
          their v04 versions remain authoritative until the next pass.

